WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:04.890
Oberyn Martell: For centuries, the Iron Throne
had no more loyal ally than the Princes of

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:05.930
Dorne.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:10.280
Since the Martells had never fallen to them,
we kept our ancestral title.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.949
Perhaps this is what drew Rhaegar Targaryen
to us.

00:00:13.949 --> 00:00:18.120
His royal parents had not produced a sister
for him to wed, so he had to look elsewhere

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:23.610
for a princess, and there was only one in
Westeros.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:28.289
Elia of House Martell, my sister.

00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:31.940
She was not the most beautiful woman in the
world or even in Dorne.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:38.710
But, rare for a woman from our land, her flower
came with no thorns.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:41.930
She was kind and clever with a gentle heart.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.399
I loved her.

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:45.510
I feared for her.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.470
For years, I fended off lesser men from her.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:52.290
But when Rhaegar came, even I failed.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:56.170
He was beautiful, and the crown prince of
the Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.800
And our mother had worked so hard to secure
the match.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.270
How could Elia not accept it?

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:06.810
They were wed, and he took Elia from her home,
from those who loved her and would die for

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:14.979
her and locked her in his Red Keep above his
sty of a city surrounded by false friends.

00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:20.240
She bore him a daughter and a son, though
each almost cost her her life.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:26.999
Elia loved Rhaegar, she obeyed him, and he
chose to steal away Lyanna Stark, a pale northern

00:01:26.999 --> 00:01:30.579
girl whose veins ran with ice like all of
her people.

00:01:30.579 --> 00:01:35.649
Instead of disciplining his faithless son,
King Aerys executed the Starks when they came

00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:39.399
seeking justice and ignited a revolt.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:44.090
I know how the maesters describe the war now
but calling it "Robert's Rebellion" does not

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.159
change what it was.

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:49.319
The War of the Usurper.

00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:54.279
Dorne sided with the Crown, for when we swear
oaths, we keep them.

00:01:54.279 --> 00:01:59.139
We needed no threats from King Aerys, though
he made them anyway, locking Elia and her

00:01:59.139 --> 00:02:03.039
children in the Red Keep to ensure our loyalty.

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:07.380
Even in his madness, he knew that no true
Dornishman would ever take up arms against

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:12.700
our beloved princess and that we would fight
to the death for whatever side she was on.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:18.410
Barristan Selmy: A plan was devised; Prince
Rhaegar would personally lead the royal forces,

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:23.610
now reinforced with ten thousand Dornishmen,
north to face Robert, while the Kingsguard,

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.650
Lewyn Martell and I, would ride with the prince.

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:32.140
Oberyn Martell: At the Trident, Dorne lost
ten thousand men and two princes.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:39.360
My uncle in the Kingsguard and Elia's gallant
husband Prince Rhaegar, who was too slow or

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:42.950
too arrogant for Robert's war hammer.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:48.300
As Robert's army marched on King's Landing,
the Mad King sent his own wife and child away

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.600
but kept my sister and hers inside.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.230
In his madness, Aerys thought the Dornish
had betrayed his son at the Trident and was

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:01.330
only too happy to welcome his one true friend
back into his ranks.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:05.200
Tywin Lannister.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:10.420
Lord Tywin's army sacked his friend's city
while Lord Tywin's son murdered the king he

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.720
had sworn to protect.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.070
All of this could have been forgiven.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:19.570
War is terrible, and men must become terrible
to wage it.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:25.130
But the Lannisters knew that as long as Elia
and her children, Prince Rhaegar's heirs,

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:29.900
lived, no usurper could safely sit the Throne.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:37.260
So Lord Tywin's dog, "Ser" Gregor Clegane,
the Mountain, made Elia watch as he murdered

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:42.990
her daughter and dashed her infant son's head
against a wall.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:48.510
Then with her baby's blood still on his hands,
he murdered her.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:52.890
When Lord Tywin later presented their bodies
to Robert Baratheon wrapped in pretty Lannister

00:03:52.890 --> 00:04:00.420
cloaks, I have been told the red color graciously
hid the blood from men's eyes.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.459
The Targaryens talk of fire and blood.

00:04:03.459 --> 00:04:07.210
In Dorne, our blood is fire.

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:11.490
If Robert Baratheon had dared set foot in
Dorne during his reign, he would have lost

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.490
the foot.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:17.389
When I was a boy of sixteen, a great lord
caught me with his mistress.

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:18.449
He should have been honored.

00:04:18.449 --> 00:04:22.800
Instead, the fat old fool challenged me to
a duel.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.060
Thanks to my age and status, only to first
blood.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:32.880
But his mistress, and his wife, warned me
which of my parts he intended to draw first

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.990
blood from.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:36.900
He was strong and fierce but slow.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.639
I cut him quickly, and the duel ended with
honor satisfied.

00:04:40.639 --> 00:04:44.499
Then, his wounds festered, and he died.

00:04:44.499 --> 00:04:51.380
Ever since, men have called me "the Red Viper,"
a name that never fails to draw a laugh from

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:52.380
me.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:55.370
As if a single serpent was all he knew of
venom.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.930
Varys: Westeros has mighty rivers, but none
of them compare to the Rhoyne.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:05.779
It is said that there is no stream or puddle
in western Essos but drains to Mother Rhoyne.

00:05:05.779 --> 00:05:09.990
No doubt, an exaggeration.Until one sees the
river.

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:14.669
At its widest, a man in the center can't see
a shore to either side.

00:05:14.669 --> 00:05:19.330
The greatest of Mother Rhoyne's children were
the Rhoynar, a civilization as ancient and

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.029
grand as Old Ghis.

00:05:21.029 --> 00:05:26.270
Fishers, traders, scholars, workers of wood,
stone, and metal, the Rhoynar raised their

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:31.229
elegant cities from the headwaters of the
Rhoyne down to her mouth, each lovelier than

00:05:31.229 --> 00:05:32.229
the last.

00:05:32.229 --> 00:05:35.699
For many centuries, the Rhoynar lived in relative
peace.

00:05:35.699 --> 00:05:41.110
When invaders swept down from the hills, the
Rhoynar women and men would don silver-scaled

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:46.360
armor, fish head helms, tall spears, and turtle
shell shields.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:50.979
If the enemy did not laugh themselves away,
it was said that Mother Rhoyne would whisper

00:05:50.979 --> 00:05:56.240
the enemy's secrets to her children, and the
Rhoynish wizards could raise watery walls

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.559
to drown their foes.

00:05:58.559 --> 00:06:02.150
Whatever magic the Rhoynar may have had, it
wasn't enough.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:06.789
When Valyrian colonists first arrived, the
Rhoynar embraced them, for all men were welcome

00:06:06.789 --> 00:06:09.639
to share the bounty of Mother Rhoyne.

00:06:09.639 --> 00:06:14.949
Perhaps a water people should have been more
cautious of strangers who exulted fire and

00:06:14.949 --> 00:06:15.949
blood.

00:06:15.949 --> 00:06:21.360
Legend has it that one day the Valyrians netted
and butchered one of the giant turtles the

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.860
Rhoynar held sacred.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:29.360
As a result, thousands were killed or enslaved,
cities and towns were burned, drowned, and

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.360
rebuilt.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:34.199
In these wars, the Valyrians emerged as victorious
more often than not.

00:06:34.199 --> 00:06:39.229
The princes of the Rhoynish cities, fiercely
proud of their independence, fought alone,

00:06:39.229 --> 00:06:42.539
whilst the Valyrian colonies aided one another.

00:06:42.539 --> 00:06:47.919
Eventually, the Rhoynish princes ceased their
squabbling and united behind Prince Garin,

00:06:47.919 --> 00:06:54.811
who led the largest army Essos had ever seen
against 100,000 Valyrian colonists, 100 war

00:06:54.811 --> 00:06:58.469
elephants, and three dragonlords.

00:06:58.469 --> 00:07:02.870
Thousands burned, but thousands more sheltered
in the shallows of the river whilst the Rhoynish

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:07.949
wizards raised enormous water spouts against
the foes' dragons.

00:07:07.949 --> 00:07:14.300
Rhoynish archers brought down two of the dragons
whilst the third fled wounded, and thereafter

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.180
the Rhoynar named Garin "the Great."

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:21.419
But Mother Valyria proved just as caring as
Mother Rhoyne.

00:07:21.419 --> 00:07:27.129
When Garin the Great marched his army against
Volantis, three hundred Valyrian dragons descended

00:07:27.129 --> 00:07:28.449
from the sky.

00:07:28.449 --> 00:07:31.919
Tens of thousands burned whilst others rushed
into the river.

00:07:31.919 --> 00:07:36.360
But the fire burned so hot that the waters
boiled and turned to steam.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:41.089
Garin the Great was captured alive and made
to watch as Valyrians butchered every last

00:07:41.089 --> 00:07:46.249
man, so many that their blood turned the great
harbor of Volantis red as far as the eye could

00:07:46.249 --> 00:07:47.249
see.

00:07:47.249 --> 00:07:51.860
Then they forced Garin to watch as they marched
on his own city and enslaved all the women

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:54.660
and children his army had left behind.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:59.780
The singers claimed that Prince Garin called
out Mother Rhoyne to curse the Valyrians,

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:04.370
and she, in turn, flooded the city with foul
waters and a damp fog that caused the skin

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:09.360
of the Valyrians to harden and crack, and
thus was born greyscale.

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:15.999
Fearing a similar fate, another Rhoynish ruler,
Princess Nymeria, led her own people into

00:08:15.999 --> 00:08:20.930
every ship, skiff, and raft they had and fled
Essos.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:26.939
Eventually, after much hardship, they landed
in sunswept and bone dry Dorne.

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:29.149
But we all know that tale.

00:08:29.149 --> 00:08:33.860
Oberyn Martell: She was lucky to land in Dorne,
where powerful women are not locked away in

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.880
septs and the beds of old men.

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:43.020
My ancestor, Mors Martell, saw her and desired
her, and proved that where armies fail, a

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:45.110
tongue may succeed.

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:53.190
Wedding his strength to hers, his spear to
her sun, they subdued all of his rivals together.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:59.060
After the tradition of her people, House Martell
then ruled Dorne as Princes, not kings, unless

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:01.140
the eldest child was a daughter.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.130
For unlike the rest of Westeros, our loyalty
is not commanded by a cock.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:08.840
We follow a Prince or a Princess Martell just
the same, and we always have.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:15.050
Some people forget that Aegon Targaryen crowned
himself lord of six kingdoms, not seven.

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:20.611
When his sister marched on Dorne, she found
no mighty hosts drawn up against her for her

00:09:20.611 --> 00:09:23.490
dragon to burn and her soldiers to slaughter.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:27.400
The sands swirled, men died, and her dragon
saw nothing.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:33.830
The sun shone, men died, and her dragon bowed
to our greater fire.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:39.340
The Targaryens retreated with their tails
tucked between their legs.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:42.300
Of course, in later years, his descendants
would try again.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:49.350
Daeron the First succeeded at great cost and
reigned in Dorne for a few glorious months.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:53.630
One night, his steward pulled down a sash
by his bed to summon his consorts.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:59.140
Instead, the canopy split open, and a hundred
red scorpions fell on him.

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:00.530
He was a Tyrell.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:03.400
You would think he would be used to getting
stung.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:12.450
Within a fortnight, House Martell again ruled
a free Dorne.

